# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:154
msgid "Locus Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto Locus"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:154
msgid ""
"The pinnacle of artificer tradecraft, these amulets wrought in platinum and set with a perfect sapphire can contain enchantments of nearly unimaginable potency."
msgstr ""
"La cumbre del oficio de los artífices: estos amuletos labrados en platino y engastados con un zafiro perfecto pueden contener encantamientos de una potencia casi inimaginable."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:155 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:156 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:157
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:158 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:159
msgid ""
"The primitive materials of this wand is infused with dark spiritual energy. To use this wand, you must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Los toscos materiales de esta varita están imbuidos de una oscura energía espiritual. Para usar esta varita, debéis equiparla como si fuera un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:155
msgid "Witch's Wand of Fire"
msgstr "Varita de Fuego de Bruja"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:156
msgid "Witch's Wand of Sparks"
msgstr "Varita de Chispas de Bruja"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:157
msgid "Witch's Wand of Poison"
msgstr "Varita de Veneno de Bruja"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1577
msgid "Catalyst potion"
msgstr "Poción catalizadora"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:158
msgid "Witch's Wand of Stunning"
msgstr "Varita Aturdidora de Bruja"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:159
msgid "Witch's Wand of Harming"
msgstr "Varita Dañina de Bruja"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:16
msgid "Lizardman Broadsword"
msgstr "Espada Ancha de Hombre-Lagarto"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:16
msgid "The Lizardmen produce a weapon capable of giving sturdy service."
msgstr ""
"Los hombres-lagarto fabrican un arma capaz de prestar un servicio robusto."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:160
msgid "Shaman's Wand of Light"
msgstr "Varita de Luz de Chamán"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:160 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:161 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:162
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:163 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:164
msgid ""
"Something rattles ominously within the gog skull topping this wand - product of Ogre mage magic. To use it, you must equip it like a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Algo resuena ominosamente dentro del cráneo de gog que corona esta varita, fruto de la magia de los ogros brujos. Para usarla, debéis equiparla como un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1606
msgid "Of simple make and design, this longsword is deadly nonetheless."
msgstr ""
"De factura y diseño sencillos, esta espada larga no deja de ser mortífera."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1607
msgid "A longsword of superior strength and edge."
msgstr "Una espada larga de resistencia y filo superiores."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1607
msgid "Warrior Sword"
msgstr "Espada de Guerrero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1608
msgid "Crusader Sword"
msgstr "Espada de Cruzado"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1608
msgid ""
"Hammered metal patterns on the blade of this longsword suggest high quality Dwarven manufacture."
msgstr ""
"Los dibujos de metal martillado en la hoja de esta espada larga delatan una fabricación enana de gran calidad."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1609
msgid ""
"An extremely high quality longsword, this weapon is one of no more than one thousand of its kind forged by master weaponsmith Mekorig the Blind circa 780-800."
msgstr ""
"Una espada larga de altísima calidad; esta arma es una de las apenas mil de su clase forjadas por el maestro armero Mekorig el Ciego hacia los años 780-800."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1609
msgid "Conqueror Sword"
msgstr "Espada de Conquistador"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:161
msgid "Shaman's Wand of Ice"
msgstr "Varita de Hielo de Chamán"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1610
msgid ""
"A weapon as rare as it is ancient, this longsword was forged during the Time of Wonders.  The process used to forge steel of this quality was lost sometime just after the Silence."
msgstr ""
"Un arma tan rara como antigua: esta espada larga fue forjada durante la Época de las Maravillas.  El método para forjar acero de esta calidad se perdió poco después del Silencio."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1610
msgid "Lionheart Sword"
msgstr "Espada Corazón de León"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1611
msgid ""
"A basic two-handed sword.  Thousands of these low quality weapons can be found throughout Enroth."
msgstr ""
"Un mandoble corriente.  Miles de estas armas de baja calidad pueden encontrarse por todo Enroth."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1611
msgid "Claymore"
msgstr "Mandoble"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1612
msgid "Barbarian Flamberge"
msgstr "Flamberga Bárbara"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1612
msgid ""
"Yet another simple two-handed sword, this barbarian's weapon sports a wavy blade and an extra cross piece.  Its construction is sturdy and the blade is sharp."
msgstr ""
"Otro sencillo mandoble más; esta arma de bárbaro luce una hoja ondulada y un gavilán adicional.  Su construcción es sólida y la hoja está afilada."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1613
msgid ""
"An unusually high quality two-handed sword, this blade is both strong and reliable."
msgstr ""
"Un mandoble de una calidad inusualmente alta; esta hoja es fuerte y fiable a la vez."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1613
msgid "Vanquisher Sword"
msgstr "Espada del Vencedor"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1614
msgid ""
"A common broadsword.  These blades can be found throughout the land in the hands of both heroes and villains."
msgstr ""
"Una espada ancha común.  Estas hojas pueden encontrarse por todas partes, en manos tanto de héroes como de villanos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1614
msgid "Fine Broadsword"
msgstr "Espada Ancha Fina"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1615
msgid ""
"A larger variety of the Erathian steel broadsword, not a bit inferior in quality to its smaller counterpart. The increased size requires more strength to wield, but it's guaranteed to leave a mark."
msgstr ""
"Una variante más grande de la espada ancha de acero de Erathia, en nada inferior en calidad a su hermana menor. Su mayor tamaño exige más fuerza para blandirla, pero deja huella sin falta."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1615
msgid "Massive Steel Broadsword"
msgstr "Espada Ancha Maciza de Acero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1616
msgid "Mighty Broadsword"
msgstr "Espada Ancha Poderosa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1616
msgid ""
"This broadsword's edge and beauty are enchanted and untouched by time.  The blade looks as though it was forged yesterday."
msgstr ""
"El filo y la belleza de esta espada ancha están encantados y el tiempo no los ha tocado.  La hoja parece forjada ayer mismo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1617
msgid ""
"A cutlass of Goblin manufacture, this blade is as deadly as it is ugly."
msgstr "Un alfanje de factura goblin; esta hoja es tan mortífera como fea."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1618
msgid "Pirate Cutlass"
msgstr "Alfanje Pirata"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1618
msgid ""
"The traditional back-up weapon of the Regnan pirates living on the countless islands east of the island of Mist.  These cutlasses were forged by one of a long line of smiths native to those islands."
msgstr ""
"El arma de reserva tradicional de los piratas de Regna que habitan las incontables islas al este de la isla de Mist.  Estos alfanjes los forjó uno de los miembros de un largo linaje de herreros nativos de esas islas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1619
msgid "Master Cutlass"
msgstr "Alfanje de Maestro"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1619
msgid ""
"These splendid cutlasses were created in limited numbers by Alec Teling, master armorer to Hareck IX, and were issued only to admirals of Regnan fleets as a symbol of station. You are not likely to set your eyes upon a finer cutlass in your lifetime."
msgstr ""
"Estos espléndidos alfanjes los creó en número limitado Alec Teling, maestro armero de Hareck IX, y solo se entregaban a los almirantes de las flotas de Regna como símbolo de su rango. Difícilmente veréis un alfanje mejor en toda vuestra vida."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:162
msgid "Shaman's Wand of Lashing"
msgstr "Varita Azotadora de Chamán"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1620
msgid "A common dagger, favorite of thieves and assassins the world over."
msgstr "Una daga común, la favorita de ladrones y asesinos de todo el mundo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1621
msgid "Blood Dagger"
msgstr "Daga de Sangre"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1621
msgid ""
"Blood Daggers are ceremonial weapons worn by the nobility of Regna.  Their popularity has spread in recent years to the nobility of Enroth, and now they can be found throughout the land.  Though ceremonial, they are sharp and reliable blades."
msgstr ""
"Las Dagas de Sangre son armas ceremoniales que lleva la nobleza de Regna.  En los últimos años su popularidad se ha extendido a la nobleza de Enroth, y ahora pueden encontrarse por todo el país.  Aunque ceremoniales, son hojas afiladas y fiables."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1622
msgid ""
"Commissioned by Ethric the Mad while still a human, it is said these daggers have a link to the Land of the Dead.  They are used in certain magical rituals designed to extend life to unnatural lengths."
msgstr ""
"Encargadas por Ethric el Loco cuando aún era humano, se dice que estas dagas tienen un vínculo con la Tierra de los Muertos.  Se usan en ciertos rituales mágicos destinados a prolongar la vida hasta extremos antinaturales."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1622
msgid "Shadow Dagger"
msgstr "Daga de las Sombras"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1623
msgid "Mage Dagger"
msgstr "Daga de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1623
msgid ""
"One of less than a hundred such blades, Mage daggers were carried and forged by members of the Alchemical Alliance roughly 300 years ago in the fires beneath Castle Alamos.  It is no longer possible to make a finer blade than a Mage dagger."
msgstr ""
"Una de menos de cien hojas semejantes; las dagas de mago las forjaron y llevaron los miembros de la Alianza Alquímica hace unos 300 años, en los fuegos que arden bajo el Castillo Alamos.  Ya no es posible fabricar una hoja mejor que una daga de mago."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1624
msgid ""
"A weapon from the Time of Wonders, this blade is of both extreme age and quality."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de la Época de las Maravillas; esta hoja es tan antigua como excelente."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1624
msgid "Jeweled Dagger"
msgstr "Daga Enjoyada"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1625
msgid "Fine Long Dagger"
msgstr "Daga Larga Fina"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1625
msgid ""
"The common long dagger.  Bordering on swords, these long daggers are favored by assassins who want a weapon that is both concealable yet has a longer reach than the traditional dagger."
msgstr ""
"La daga larga común.  Casi espadas, estas dagas largas son las preferidas de los asesinos que buscan un arma fácil de ocultar pero con más alcance que la daga tradicional."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1626
msgid "Piercing Dagger"
msgstr "Daga Perforadora"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1626
msgid ""
"Really more of a short sword than a dagger, the narrow blade belies an unusual strength and a possibly enchanted edge."
msgstr ""
"Más espada corta que daga, su estrecha hoja oculta una fuerza inusual y un filo posiblemente encantado."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1627
msgid ""
"A 'Weapon of the Gods', this weapon was one of the last created before the great forges fell to the Silence in the year 113 A.S (After the Silence)."
msgstr ""
"Un «Arma de los Dioses»: fue una de las últimas creadas antes de que las grandes forjas cayeran con el Silencio en el año 113 D.S. (Después del Silencio)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1627
msgid "Divine Dagger"
msgstr "Daga Divina"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1628
msgid "Hand Axe"
msgstr "Hacha de Mano"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1628
msgid ""
"More of a tool than a weapon, this simple axe will work in a pinch.  But don't expect much."
msgstr ""
"Más herramienta que arma, esta sencilla hacha os sacará de un apuro.  Pero no esperéis mucho de ella."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1629
msgid "Barbarian Axe"
msgstr "Hacha Bárbara"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1629
msgid ""
"Made as a weapon of war instead of a tool, this  battle axe is usually employed by barbarians and undisciplined armies."
msgstr ""
"Hecha como arma de guerra y no como herramienta, esta hacha de batalla suelen emplearla los bárbaros y los ejércitos indisciplinados."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:163
msgid "Shaman's Wand of Mind"
msgstr "Varita de la Mente de Chamán"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1630
msgid ""
"This War Axe appears to be one of a large shipment of such axes seized by Roland during the Succession War.  It was manufactured in Karigor by order of Archibald Ironfist to be used against his brother in their struggle for the throne of Enroth."
msgstr ""
"Esta Hacha de Guerra parece formar parte de un gran cargamento de hachas semejantes que Roland requisó durante la Guerra de Sucesión.  Se fabricó en Karigor por orden de Archibald Ironfist para usarla contra su hermano en su lucha por el trono de Enroth."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1630
msgid "War Axe"
msgstr "Hacha de Guerra"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1631
msgid ""
"An example of the high quality work done by the dwarves of the Red Mountains, the blade is sharp and the balance perfect."
msgstr ""
"Una muestra del trabajo de gran calidad de los enanos de las Montañas Rojas: la hoja está afilada y el equilibrio es perfecto."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1631
msgid "Dwarven Noble Axe"
msgstr "Hacha de Noble Enano"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1632
msgid "Supreme Axe"
msgstr "Hacha Suprema"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1632
msgid ""
"This weapon surely has a dark history.  An axe of this quality is only forged as the personal weapon of a noble Dwarf, and it is never sold or traded away…"
msgstr ""
"Esta arma tiene sin duda una historia oscura.  Un hacha de esta calidad solo se forja como arma personal de un noble enano, y jamás se vende ni se cambia…"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1633
msgid "Light Poleaxe"
msgstr "Hacha de Asta Ligera"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1633
msgid ""
"This style of long hafted axe is typically used to deadly effect by Eastern tribes and the elite guard of some members of the nobility."
msgstr ""
"Este tipo de hacha de mango largo la emplean con efectos mortíferos las tribus del Este y la guardia de élite de algunos nobles."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1634
msgid ""
"A stronger version of the basic Poleaxe, this weapon is frequently used by city guards and other fighters who don't expect to do battle in large, coordinated groups (like armies)."
msgstr ""
"Una versión más robusta del Hacha de Asta básica; esta arma la usan a menudo los guardias de las ciudades y otros combatientes que no esperan luchar en grandes grupos coordinados (como los ejércitos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1634
msgid "Heavy Poleaxe"
msgstr "Hacha de Asta Pesada"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1635
msgid "Grand Poleaxe"
msgstr "Gran Hacha de Asta"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1635
msgid ""
"The blade head of this weapon was obviously created with the aid of magic.  It is both unusually sharp and light at the same time."
msgstr ""
"La hoja de esta arma se creó claramente con ayuda de la magia.  Es inusualmente afilada y ligera a la vez."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1636
msgid ""
"Barely more than a sharpened stick, this spear is still quite deadly.  Like all spears, it can be used in one or both hands (+1D9 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Poco más que un palo afilado, esta lanza no deja de ser bastante mortífera.  Como todas las lanzas, puede usarse con una o con ambas manos (+1D9 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1637
msgid "Stout Spear"
msgstr "Lanza Robusta"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1637
msgid ""
"This spear has a reinforced steel tip to help it penetrate tough armor and hides.  Like all spears, it can be used in one or both hands (+1D9 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Esta lanza tiene una punta de acero reforzado que la ayuda a atravesar armaduras y pieles duras.  Como todas las lanzas, puede usarse con una o con ambas manos (+1D9 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1638
msgid ""
"Decorated with carved serpents running along the shaft, this spear comes equipped with a cross piece designed to prevent impaled foes from sliding along the shaft of the spear and striking a blow at you as they die.  Like all spears, it can be used in one or both hands (+1D9 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Decorada con serpientes talladas a lo largo del asta, esta lanza lleva un travesaño pensado para impedir que los enemigos ensartados se deslicen por el asta y os asesten un golpe mientras mueren.  Como todas las lanzas, puede usarse con una o con ambas manos (+1D9 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1638
msgid "Serpent Spear"
msgstr "Lanza de la Serpiente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1639
msgid ""
"Composed entirely of a rare, bluish metal, the lower half of this spear is wrapped in an expensive leather.  A collector's item!  Like all spears, it can be used in one or both hands (+1D9 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Hecha por completo de un raro metal azulado, la mitad inferior de esta lanza está envuelta en un cuero caro.  ¡Una pieza de coleccionista!  Como todas las lanzas, puede usarse con una o con ambas manos (+1D9 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1639
msgid "Savage Spear"
msgstr "Lanza Salvaje"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:164
msgid "Shaman's Wand of Swarms"
msgstr "Varita de Enjambres de Chamán"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1640
msgid "Sacred Spear"
msgstr "Lanza Sagrada"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1640
msgid ""
"This spear bears characteristics of equipment from the Time of Wonders - beautiful, in perfect condition and lethal. This model was already produced centuries before the Silence and remained in production almost towards the end of the Heavenly Forges, in that period serving ceremonial and representative purposes. Later combat models are the only mass-produced spears that surpass these in any capacity (+1D9 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Esta lanza tiene las características del equipo de la Época de las Maravillas: bella, en perfecto estado y letal. Este modelo ya se fabricaba siglos antes del Silencio y siguió produciéndose casi hasta el final de las Forjas Celestiales, época en la que cumplía fines ceremoniales y de representación. Solo los modelos de combate posteriores son lanzas fabricadas en serie que las superan en algún aspecto (+1D9 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1641
msgid ""
"Combination poleax and spear, the halberd can inflict terrible wounds, but recovers slowly from swings.  This one is of average quality and workmanship (+1D6 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Combinación de hacha de asta y lanza, la alabarda puede infligir heridas terribles, pero se recupera despacio tras cada golpe.  Esta es de calidad y factura corrientes (+1D6 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1641
msgid "Common Halberd"
msgstr "Alabarda Común"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1642
msgid "Massive Halberd"
msgstr "Alabarda Maciza"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1642
msgid ""
"Of solid construction, this halberd has a particularly heavy blade.  Wielded by a mighty warrior, it could surely be used to slay the toughest of monsters (+1D6 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"De construcción sólida, esta alabarda tiene una hoja especialmente pesada.  En manos de un guerrero poderoso, sin duda podría abatir a los monstruos más duros (+1D6 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1643
msgid "Elite Halberd"
msgstr "Alabarda de Élite"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1643
msgid ""
"That this magnificent halberd is a product of the Mekorig Foundry comes as no surprise to you. From the intricate shape of the head to the sturdiness of the construction -- everything about this weapon screams quality (+1D6 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"No os sorprende que esta magnífica alabarda sea obra de la Fundición Mekorig. Desde la intrincada forma de la hoja hasta la solidez de su construcción, todo en esta arma pregona calidad (+1D6 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1644
msgid ""
"Common war tridents, like this one, are good quality weapons issued by the Imperial Regnan Navy to facilitate the collection of Imperial tariffs on the high seas.  Most merchants and other governments refer to this activity as piracy…(+1D6 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Los tridentes de guerra comunes, como este, son armas de buena calidad que la Armada Imperial de Regna entrega para facilitar el cobro de los aranceles imperiales en alta mar.  La mayoría de los mercaderes y de los demás gobiernos llaman a esta actividad piratería… (+1D6 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1645
msgid ""
"A high quality war trident of the style given to officers of the Imperial Regnan Navy.  This one was probably taken from the officer during an Imperial Taxation battle that went poorly for the Navy (+1D6 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Un tridente de guerra de gran calidad, del estilo que se entrega a los oficiales de la Armada Imperial de Regna.  Probablemente se lo arrebataron a su oficial durante una batalla de Recaudación Imperial que acabó mal para la Armada (+1D6 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1645
msgid "Ornate Trident"
msgstr "Tridente Ornamentado"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1646
msgid ""
"This beautiful trident is mostly made of Kergar, a rare, bluish metal that does not rust or lose its edge over time (+1D6 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""
"Este hermoso tridente está hecho casi por completo de kergar, un raro metal azulado que no se oxida ni pierde el filo con el tiempo (+1D6 si se usa a dos manos)."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1646
msgid "Titanic Trident"
msgstr "Tridente Titánico"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1647
msgid "Crude Longbow"
msgstr "Arco Largo Tosco"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1648
msgid ""
"A weapon only made by the Elves of the great Erathian forests.  This one reflects the same high quality workmanship found in all Elvish artifacts."
msgstr ""
"Un arma que solo fabrican los elfos de los grandes bosques de Erathia.  Este refleja la misma factura de gran calidad que se encuentra en todos los objetos élficos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1648
msgid "Elven Bow"
msgstr "Arco Élfico"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1649
msgid ""
"Etched initials at the base of the bow indicate this bow was made by master bowyer Ivan Selving's workshop during the Timber Wars against the Elves of Erathia in the late 600's."
msgstr ""
"Las iniciales grabadas en la base del arco indican que se fabricó en el taller del maestro arquero Ivan Selving durante las Guerras de la Madera contra los elfos de Erathia, a finales del siglo VII."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1649
msgid "Precision Bow"
msgstr "Arco de Precisión"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:165 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:166 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:167
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:168 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:169
msgid ""
"A wand of highly polished thornbark wrapped with platinum wire. To use it, you must equip it like a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una varita de corteza espinosa muy pulida y envuelta en hilo de platino. Para usarla, debéis equiparla como un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:165
msgid "Wizard Wand of Fireballs"
msgstr "Varita de Bolas de Fuego de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1650
msgid "Magic Bow"
msgstr "Arco Mágico"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1650
msgid ""
"This bow is composed of strange materials and bound together by subtle enchantments.  It is extremely light and accurate."
msgstr ""
"Este arco está hecho de materiales extraños unidos mediante sutiles encantamientos.  Es extremadamente ligero y preciso."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1651
msgid ""
"Created by stripping the Heavenly Forges of their enchanted parts when they became useless some years after the Silence, very few of these bows have survived the passage of time.  What few remain are hoarded by the Elves and individual collectors."
msgstr ""
"Fabricados despojando a las Forjas Celestiales de sus piezas encantadas cuando quedaron inservibles unos años después del Silencio, muy pocos de estos arcos han sobrevivido al paso del tiempo.  Los pocos que quedan los acaparan los elfos y algunos coleccionistas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1651
msgid "Stellar Bow"
msgstr "Arco Estelar"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1652
msgid ""
"Crossbows are the deadliest ranged weapons made since the Time of Wonders.  This crossbow is made of stout Yew wood and metal fixtures, but is otherwise rather ordinary."
msgstr ""
"Las ballestas son las armas a distancia más mortíferas fabricadas desde la Época de las Maravillas.  Esta ballesta está hecha de recia madera de tejo y herrajes metálicos, pero por lo demás es bastante corriente."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1653
msgid "Accurate Crossbow"
msgstr "Ballesta Precisa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1653
msgid ""
"These crossbows feature a section of curved wood next to the bowstaves, which helps prevent recoil, increasing their accuracy. It comes at the cost of a greater weight than that of lighter crossbows."
msgstr ""
"Estas ballestas llevan una pieza de madera curvada junto a las palas del arco, que ayuda a evitar el retroceso y aumenta su precisión. A cambio, pesan más que las ballestas más ligeras."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1654
msgid ""
"Equipped with a hand crank and shaft sights, these exceptional crossbows are superior to all that have come before.  Just where they are coming from is a mystery at this time…"
msgstr ""
"Equipadas con una manivela y miras en la caja, estas ballestas excepcionales superan a todas las anteriores.  De dónde proceden es, por ahora, un misterio…"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1654
msgid "True Crossbow"
msgstr "Ballesta Verdadera"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1655
msgid ""
"Little more than a glorified club, this common mace is made of ordinary materials and unexceptional craftsmanship."
msgstr ""
"Poco más que una porra con pretensiones, esta maza común está hecha de materiales corrientes y con una factura nada excepcional."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1655
msgid "Simple Mace"
msgstr "Maza Sencilla"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1656
msgid ""
"Solidly designed to inflict fatal injuries, even through armor.  The balance is a little top heavy, but the craftsmanship is good."
msgstr ""
"De diseño sólido para infligir heridas mortales, incluso a través de la armadura.  Tiene el peso algo cargado hacia la cabeza, pero la factura es buena."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1656
msgid "Wicked Mace"
msgstr "Maza Malvada"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1657
msgid ""
"This mace is one of thousands turned out by the Heavenly Forges before the Silence.  But that was more than a thousand years ago, and not many remain."
msgstr ""
"Esta maza es una de las miles que produjeron las Forjas Celestiales antes del Silencio.  Pero de eso hace más de mil años, y no quedan muchas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1657
msgid "Thunder Mace"
msgstr "Maza del Trueno"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1658
msgid ""
"Only magic could make such an ungainly weapon so light and yet hit so hard."
msgstr ""
"Solo la magia podría hacer que un arma tan desgarbada fuera tan ligera y golpeara tan fuerte."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1658
msgid "Wonder Mace"
msgstr "Maza Prodigiosa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1659
msgid ""
"Constructed by the Necromancer's guild just prior to their fall during the Succession War, these unusual weapons are almost always enchanted with powerful magics."
msgstr ""
"Fabricadas por el Gremio de los Nigromantes justo antes de su caída durante la Guerra de Sucesión, estas armas inusuales casi siempre están encantadas con magias poderosas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1659
msgid "Death Mace"
msgstr "Maza de la Muerte"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:166
msgid "Wizard Wand of Acid"
msgstr "Varita de Ácido de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1660
msgid ""
"A graceless and unimaginative weapon, hammers are slow, but hit very hard.  This one is of common construction and materials."
msgstr ""
"Armas toscas y sin imaginación, los martillos son lentos, pero golpean muy fuerte.  Este es de construcción y materiales corrientes."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1660
msgid "Massive Hammer"
msgstr "Martillo Macizo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1661
msgid ""
"A step up in construction quality, these hammers are commonly wielded by humanoid monsters.  Since everyone knows most monsters don't make weapons, the question 'from where are they getting them?' arises…"
msgstr ""
"Un paso adelante en calidad de construcción; estos martillos los suelen empuñar los monstruos humanoides.  Como todo el mundo sabe que la mayoría de los monstruos no fabrican armas, surge la pregunta: «¿de dónde las sacan?»…"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1661
msgid "Dark Hammer"
msgstr "Martillo Oscuro"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1662
msgid "Holy Hammer"
msgstr "Martillo Sagrado"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1662
msgid ""
"Magically constructed, these hammers are the property of the Church of the Moon in Karigor."
msgstr ""
"Construidos mediante magia, estos martillos son propiedad de la Iglesia de la Luna de Karigor."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1663
msgid ""
"A primitive weapon usable by even the stupidest of monsters.  You're not thinking of using this, are you?"
msgstr ""
"Un arma primitiva que hasta el más estúpido de los monstruos sabe usar.  No estaréis pensando en usarla, ¿verdad?"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1663
msgid "Root Club"
msgstr "Porra de Raíz"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1664
msgid ""
"An improvement over the simple club, this spiked club will inflict nastier wounds."
msgstr ""
"Una mejora sobre la porra sencilla: esta porra con pinchos infligirá heridas más feas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1664
msgid "Spiked Club"
msgstr "Porra con Pinchos"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1665
msgid "Killer Club"
msgstr "Porra Asesina"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1665
msgid ""
"King of the club family.  If this weapon had a knob or ball on the end, it would be a mace.  There is evidence of real craftsmanship in this club, but you can see no true identifying marks that would indicate who created it."
msgstr ""
"La reina de la familia de las porras.  Si esta arma tuviera un pomo o una bola en el extremo, sería una maza.  En esta porra hay indicios de verdadera maestría artesana, pero no veis ninguna marca que indique quién la hizo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1666
msgid ""
"The staff is the traditional weapon of the oppressed.  This one is unremarkable, and the ruby at the end of it is actually just colored glass."
msgstr ""
"El bastón es el arma tradicional de los oprimidos.  Este no tiene nada de especial, y el rubí de su extremo es en realidad simple vidrio coloreado."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1667
msgid "Emerald Staff"
msgstr "Bastón de Esmeralda"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1667
msgid ""
"Magically light and hard, this staff is made of a rare wood stripped from the Elves during the Timber War in 600 A.S.  The emerald at the end of it is real, and probably serves as a magical reservoir from which the staff draws its strength."
msgstr ""
"Mágicamente ligero y duro, este bastón está hecho de una madera rara arrebatada a los elfos durante la Guerra de la Madera, en el 600 D.S.  La esmeralda de su extremo es auténtica y probablemente sirve de reserva mágica de la que el bastón extrae su fuerza."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1668
msgid "Power Staff"
msgstr "Bastón de Poder"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1668
msgid ""
"This staff, along with others of its kind, was found in the treasure room of the Necromancer's guild after their disastrous defeat by Roland at the end of the Succession War."
msgstr ""
"Este bastón, junto con otros de su clase, se encontró en la sala del tesoro del Gremio de los Nigromantes tras su desastrosa derrota a manos de Roland al final de la Guerra de Sucesión."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1669
msgid ""
"A weapon of awesome power, clearly created during the Time of Wonders."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de un poder asombroso, creada sin duda durante la Época de las Maravillas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:167
msgid "Wizard Wand of Lightning"
msgstr "Varita de Relámpagos de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1670
msgid ""
"The finest of personal weapons made during the Time of Wonders, this Blaster Rifle can deal death faster than any weapon you have ever seen."
msgstr ""
"La mejor arma personal fabricada durante la Época de las Maravillas: este Rifle Bláster puede repartir la muerte más rápido que cualquier arma que hayáis visto."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1671
msgid ""
"Lightest and most easily made among the armors, leather armor offers the least protection.  This particular suit is of average quality."
msgstr ""
"La más ligera y fácil de fabricar de todas las armaduras, la armadura de cuero es la que menos protege.  Esta en concreto es de calidad corriente."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1672
msgid "Reinforced Leather"
msgstr "Cuero Reforzado"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1672
msgid ""
"Studded leather offers more protection than regular leather armor at the expense of being stiffer and weighing more.  This particular suit is well made."
msgstr ""
"El cuero tachonado protege más que la armadura de cuero normal, a costa de ser más rígido y pesar más.  Esta en concreto está bien hecha."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1673
msgid ""
"A subtly enchanted suit of armor that is much stronger than its weight would suggest. Shoulder and waist pads offer added protection with no cost to freedom of movement."
msgstr ""
"Una armadura sutilmente encantada, mucho más resistente de lo que sugiere su peso. Las hombreras y las protecciones de la cintura ofrecen una protección adicional sin restar libertad de movimiento."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1673
msgid "Enchanted Leather"
msgstr "Cuero Encantado"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1674
msgid "Dragon Leather"
msgstr "Cuero de Dragón"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1674
msgid ""
"Standard issue leather armor for officers in the Regnan Navy.  All such leather armor receives enchantments to strengthen and lighten it during its creation in the Regnan Armories. This particular suit is a somewhat heavier than usual variation with a bit more body coverage."
msgstr ""
"Armadura de cuero reglamentaria de los oficiales de la Armada de Regna.  Toda armadura de cuero de este tipo recibe encantamientos que la refuerzan y la aligeran durante su fabricación en las Armerías de Regna. Esta en concreto es una variante algo más pesada de lo habitual, que cubre un poco más el cuerpo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1675
msgid ""
"An extremely rare suit of leather armor created during the conflicts between the Church of the Moon and the Church of the Sun roughly 80 years ago.  These suits provide the finest protection available with leather armor."
msgstr ""
"Una armadura de cuero extremadamente rara, creada durante los conflictos entre la Iglesia de la Luna y la Iglesia del Sol hace unos 80 años.  Estas armaduras ofrecen la mejor protección posible en armadura de cuero."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1675
msgid "Imperial Leather"
msgstr "Cuero Imperial"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1676
msgid ""
"Chain mail is an armor formed of small, interlocking loops of metal.  This suit is low quality:  the metal used is plain iron, there are only two layers of rings, and it is heavy and stiff for its size. Despite beginning to corrode, it has so far remained intact."
msgstr ""
"La cota de malla es una armadura formada por pequeñas anillas de metal entrelazadas.  Esta es de baja calidad: el metal es hierro simple, solo tiene dos capas de anillas y es pesada y rígida para su tamaño. Aunque empieza a oxidarse, de momento sigue intacta."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1677
msgid ""
"A superior suit of chain mail, the metal used in this suit is steel, and the former owner was careful to keep the suit well oiled and free of rust. Its coverage of areas below the waist could have been better, though."
msgstr ""
"Una cota de malla de calidad superior: el metal es acero, y su antiguo dueño tuvo cuidado de mantenerla bien engrasada y libre de óxido. Eso sí, podría cubrir mejor la zona por debajo de la cintura."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1677
msgid "Basic Steel Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de Malla de Acero Básica"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1678
msgid ""
"Cavalry officer's chain mail from the reign of Taledon V of Karigor, Divine High Priest and High Holy Conduit of the Church of the Sun, circa 870 A.S.  The armor is high quality chain, enchanted to lighten and strengthen the metal."
msgstr ""
"Cota de malla de oficial de caballería del reinado de Taledon V de Karigor, Divino Sumo Sacerdote y Sumo Conducto Sagrado de la Iglesia del Sol, hacia el 870 D.S.  La armadura es una malla de gran calidad, encantada para aligerar y reforzar el metal."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1678
msgid "Noble Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de Malla Noble"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1679
msgid ""
"Highly enchanted armor worn by elvish nobility and royalty during the Timber Wars of the seventh and eighth centuries."
msgstr ""
"Armadura muy encantada que llevaban la nobleza y la realeza élficas durante las Guerras de la Madera de los siglos VII y VIII."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1679
msgid "Royal Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de Malla Real"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:168
msgid "Wizard Wand of Blades"
msgstr "Varita de Cuchillas de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1680
msgid ""
"A model of armor from before the Silence -- one could see it worn by the Governor and his closest associates as a badge of office. The formula for creating these suits is quite old, in fact it was adjusted not long before the Forges broke down. As such, this chain mail is superior to most other such armors in the world today -- though still surpassed by suits created in the years just before the Silence."
msgstr ""
"Un modelo de armadura de antes del Silencio: la llevaban el Gobernador y sus allegados más cercanos como distintivo de su cargo. La fórmula para fabricar estas armaduras es bastante antigua; de hecho, se ajustó poco antes de que las Forjas dejaran de funcionar. Por eso esta cota de malla supera a la mayoría de las armaduras semejantes que existen hoy en el mundo, aunque la superan las fabricadas en los años inmediatamente anteriores al Silencio."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1680
msgid "Majestic Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de Malla Majestuosa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1681
msgid ""
"Composed of interlocking plates and joints, plate armor is the best unenchanted armor available.  It is, however, heavy and slows the movements of the wearer.  This particular suit is of average quality and the smith unknown."
msgstr ""
"Compuesta de placas y articulaciones encajadas, la armadura de placas es la mejor armadura sin encantar que existe.  Sin embargo, es pesada y entorpece los movimientos de quien la lleva.  Esta en concreto es de calidad corriente y de herrero desconocido."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1681
msgid "Plate Mail"
msgstr "Armadura de Placas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1682
msgid "Steel Plate Mail"
msgstr "Armadura de Placas de Acero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1682
msgid ""
"Well constructed plates of steel work together to form an overall excellent suit of armor.  A foundry stamp under the right arm indicates it was forged recently in Kelebrim."
msgstr ""
"Placas de acero bien construidas se combinan para formar una armadura excelente en conjunto.  Un sello de fundición bajo el brazo derecho indica que se forjó hace poco en Kelebrim."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1683
msgid "Golden Plate Mail"
msgstr "Armadura de Placas Dorada"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1683
msgid ""
"This suit of plate armor was forged in the Mekorig foundry eighteen years after the death of Mekorig the Blind.  A masterwork, the armor is almost as easy to wear as ordinary clothes, and is probably the best armor available in the world."
msgstr ""
"Esta armadura de placas se forjó en la Fundición Mekorig dieciocho años después de la muerte de Mekorig el Ciego.  Una obra maestra: es casi tan cómoda de llevar como la ropa corriente y probablemente sea la mejor armadura que existe en el mundo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1684
msgid ""
"Formed of stretched hides over a wooden frame, this simple shield provides basic protection against physical attacks."
msgstr ""
"Hecho de pieles tensadas sobre un armazón de madera, este sencillo escudo ofrece una protección básica contra los ataques físicos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1684
msgid "Kite Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de Cometa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1685
msgid ""
"The simplicity of the heraldic design on this shield leads one to believe it was created either by barbarians or goblins.  It is made of sturdy materials and should stand up reasonably well in combat."
msgstr ""
"La sencillez del diseño heráldico de este escudo hace pensar que lo fabricaron bárbaros o goblins.  Está hecho de materiales resistentes y debería aguantar bastante bien en combate."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1685
msgid "Tower Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de Torre"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1686
msgid "Castle Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de Castillo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1686
msgid ""
"This shield is made of wood framed by iron.  It is somewhat heavy for its size, but it should see you through a battle safely--as long as  you're not backstabbed."
msgstr ""
"Este escudo es de madera con un marco de hierro.  Pesa algo para su tamaño, pero debería sacaros sanos y salvos de una batalla... siempre que no os apuñalen por la espalda."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1687
msgid "Celestial Shield"
msgstr "Escudo Celestial"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1688
msgid "Olympian Shield"
msgstr "Escudo Olímpico"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1688
msgid ""
"This round shield is a design of the long gone Phynaxian empire that once ruled southern Erathia. Forged of stalt, it is extremely sturdy and susceptible to enchantments. It's so well-made that its only downside seems to be its rather compact size for a large shield, which somewhat limits its coverage."
msgstr ""
"Este escudo redondo sigue un diseño del desaparecido imperio phynaxiano que antaño gobernó el sur de Erathia. Forjado en stalt, es extremadamente resistente y admite bien los encantamientos. Está tan bien hecho que su único defecto parece ser su tamaño bastante compacto para un escudo grande, lo que limita algo lo que cubre."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1689
msgid ""
"A small wooden shield designed to protect mostly against arrows. The wood it is made of was never properly planed, making its surface full of splinters and chips. Its remaining lifetime in combat is likely much shorter than you'd like."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño escudo de madera pensado sobre todo para proteger de las flechas. La madera con que está hecho nunca se cepilló bien, así que su superficie está llena de astillas y desconchones. Lo que le queda de vida en combate será seguramente mucho menos de lo que querríais."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1689
msgid "Splintery Buckler"
msgstr "Rodela Astillada"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:169
msgid "Wizard Wand of Berzerking"
msgstr "Varita de Frenesí de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1690
msgid ""
"Bronze shields are lighter than iron shields of the same size, but aren't nearly as strong."
msgstr ""
"Los escudos de bronce son más ligeros que los de hierro del mismo tamaño, pero ni de lejos tan resistentes."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1690
msgid "Rusty Bronze Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de Bronce Oxidado"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1691
msgid ""
"Since this shield is made of tempered steel, it should resist all but the most unusual of enchanted weapons."
msgstr ""
"Como este escudo es de acero templado, debería resistir todas las armas encantadas salvo las más insólitas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1691
msgid "Steel Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de Acero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1692
msgid "Spirit Shield"
msgstr "Escudo del Espíritu"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1692
msgid ""
"Spirit shields are ordinary steel shields enchanted through a ritualistic process that can have powerful, albeit unpredictable results.  The process is time consuming and requires the undivided attention of at least three masters of Spirit magic."
msgstr ""
"Los escudos del espíritu son escudos de acero corrientes encantados mediante un proceso ritual que puede tener resultados poderosos, aunque impredecibles.  El proceso es largo y requiere la atención exclusiva de al menos tres maestros de Magia del Espíritu."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1693
msgid "Astral Shield"
msgstr "Escudo Astral"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1693
msgid ""
"These rare shields were turned out by the hundreds with the aid of the Heavenly Forges to combat rebel forces in the endless string of skirmishes and supply raids that tested (and finally overcame) the Governor's forces in the first century A.S.  As with all such equipment, it is light, tough, and is capable of holding the most powerful enchantments."
msgstr ""
"Estos raros escudos se fabricaron por cientos con ayuda de las Forjas Celestiales para combatir a las fuerzas rebeldes en la interminable serie de escaramuzas y asaltos a los suministros que pusieron a prueba (y al final vencieron) a las fuerzas del Gobernador en el primer siglo D.S.  Como todo el equipo de este tipo, es ligero, duro y capaz de albergar los encantamientos más poderosos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1694
msgid ""
"An ordinary helm.  This one is made of hides stretched over wood.  There's no fur or padding on the inside, so your head will probably ring like a bell when struck a solid blow."
msgstr ""
"Un yelmo corriente.  Este está hecho de pieles tensadas sobre madera.  No tiene pelo ni relleno por dentro, así que probablemente la cabeza os sonará como una campana si recibís un buen golpe."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1694
msgid "Wooden Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo de Madera"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1695
msgid "Steel Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo de Acero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1695
msgid ""
"This is a common steel helm.  The design is a good one and has been used for centuries by warriors all around the world.  Best guess is this helm is 50-75 years old."
msgstr ""
"Este es un yelmo de acero común.  El diseño es bueno y lo han usado durante siglos guerreros de todo el mundo.  A juzgar por su aspecto, este yelmo tiene entre 50 y 75 años."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1696
msgid "Guardian Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo de Guardián"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1696
msgid ""
"This helm design has been used by the Elves of Erathia since before the Silence. Its wing ornaments belie superior strength and add a sense of distinction for the Elven leaders who got to go into battle wearing these helms."
msgstr ""
"Los elfos de Erathia usan este diseño de yelmo desde antes del Silencio. Sus adornos en forma de alas ocultan una resistencia superior y dan un aire distinguido a los líderes élficos que tenían el honor de entrar en batalla con estos yelmos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1697
msgid "Defender Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo del Defensor"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1697
msgid ""
"Half made from the skull of the ferocious Mogred beast in Karigor, these helms grow more uncommon every year as the Mogreds approach extinction.  The red stripes around the horns of the helm are highly receptive to enchantment."
msgstr ""
"Hechos en parte con el cráneo de la feroz bestia mogred de Karigor, estos yelmos son cada año más escasos a medida que los mogreds se acercan a la extinción.  Las franjas rojas alrededor de los cuernos del yelmo son muy receptivas a los encantamientos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1698
msgid "Angelic Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo Angélico"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1698
msgid ""
"These helms are extremely rare and no one knows where they originate, but they almost certainly come from the Time of Wonders.  An extremely fine inscription inside the helm says  'Property of Ship's Store, VARN MCMIV'."
msgstr ""
"Estos yelmos son extremadamente raros y nadie sabe de dónde proceden, pero casi con certeza vienen de la Época de las Maravillas.  Una inscripción finísima en el interior del yelmo dice: «Propiedad del Almacén de la Nave, VARN MCMIV»."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1699
msgid ""
"A common hat.  The material is a blend of cotton and wool, and the feather is from a duck."
msgstr ""
"Un sombrero corriente.  El tejido es una mezcla de algodón y lana, y la pluma es de pato."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1699
msgid "Cloth Hat"
msgstr "Sombrero de Tela"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:17
msgid "Knightly Broadsword"
msgstr "Espada Ancha de Caballero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:17
msgid ""
"The weight of this sword's untapered blade would make it unwieldy if not for its exacting counterbalance."
msgstr ""
"El peso de la hoja recta de esta espada la haría difícil de manejar de no ser por su contrapeso preciso."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:170 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:171 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:172
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:173 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:174
msgid ""
"Made from the braided bodies of three snakes, this wand pulses like a slow heartbeat. To use it you must equip it like a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Hecha con los cuerpos trenzados de tres serpientes, esta varita late como un corazón lento. Para usarla, debéis equiparla como un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:170
msgid "Serpent Wand of Blasting"
msgstr "Varita Explosiva de Serpiente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1700
msgid "Dandy Hat"
msgstr "Sombrero de Petimetre"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1700
msgid ""
"Quite fashionable and stylish, these hats are in vogue amongst the upper classes and those seeking to emulate them."
msgstr ""
"Muy elegantes y a la moda, estos sombreros causan furor entre las clases altas y entre quienes intentan imitarlas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1701
msgid ""
"Don't laugh--while silly--even ridiculous--in appearance, many sorcerers spend quite a bit of time enchanting hats like this with powerful magics.  The conical shape and 'eyes' in the front of the hat are peculiarly attractive to creatures of the spirit world, and that property makes the hat easier to enchant."
msgstr ""
"No os riáis: aunque su aspecto es tonto, incluso ridículo, muchos hechiceros dedican bastante tiempo a encantar sombreros como este con magias poderosas.  La forma cónica y los «ojos» de la parte delantera atraen de manera peculiar a las criaturas del mundo de los espíritus, y esa propiedad hace que el sombrero sea más fácil de encantar."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1701
msgid "Wizard Cap"
msgstr "Gorro de Mago"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1702
msgid ""
"This is a poorly wrought crown, the kind that goblins or low budget actors might create to mock royalty.  It offers no real head protection, although it may carry some small enchantment."
msgstr ""
"Es una corona mal hecha, de las que harían los goblins o los actores de poca monta para burlarse de la realeza.  No protege realmente la cabeza, aunque puede llevar algún pequeño encantamiento."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1702
msgid "Wreath Crown"
msgstr "Corona de Guirnalda"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1703
msgid ""
"A large, imperfect sapphire is inset in the center of this delicate silver crown.  Extremely fine hammer marks suggest this crown was made by dwarven hands."
msgstr ""
"Un zafiro grande e imperfecto está engastado en el centro de esta delicada corona de plata.  Unas finísimas marcas de martillo sugieren que la hicieron manos enanas."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1703
msgid "Regal Crown"
msgstr "Corona Regia"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1704
msgid "Almighty Crown"
msgstr "Corona Todopoderosa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1704
msgid ""
"Crowns of this sort are typically created with the use of magic to enhance their susceptibility to magic.  If found with no enchantments whatsoever, the crown was probably left unfinished for some reason."
msgstr ""
"Las coronas de este tipo se fabrican normalmente con ayuda de la magia para que admitan mejor la magia.  Si se encuentra una sin ningún encantamiento, probablemente quedó sin terminar por algún motivo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1705
msgid "A common strip of leather used to hold up your pants."
msgstr "Una simple tira de cuero para sujetaros los pantalones."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1705
msgid "Crude Leather Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón de Cuero Tosco"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1706
msgid ""
"A wide leather belt with a big, flashy buckle of a kind favored by bandits and mercenaries.  Both mercenaries and bandits like to have charms or minor enchantments placed on them as battle aids."
msgstr ""
"Un cinturón de cuero ancho con una hebilla grande y llamativa, del tipo que gusta a bandidos y mercenarios.  Tanto a unos como a otros les gusta que les pongan amuletos o pequeños encantamientos como ayuda en la batalla."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1706
msgid "Mercenary Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón de Mercenario"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1707
msgid ""
"Cured dragonhide and polished bronze are fastened together to form a belt of unusual strength and resistance to magic.  Although difficult to work with, these belts can offer excellent protection against magic once an enchantment is successfully laid upon them."
msgstr ""
"Piel de dragón curtida y bronce pulido se unen para formar un cinturón de una resistencia inusual, también contra la magia.  Aunque son difíciles de trabajar, estos cinturones pueden ofrecer una excelente protección contra la magia una vez se les aplica con éxito un encantamiento."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1707
msgid "Vanguard Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón de Vanguardia"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1708
msgid ""
"Made of silver and the hide of some unknown creature, this belt is studded with vertical strips of a golden alloy.  The buckle is a single, large opal inset in a platinum base."
msgstr ""
"Hecho de plata y de la piel de alguna criatura desconocida, este cinturón está tachonado con franjas verticales de una aleación dorada.  La hebilla es un único ópalo grande engastado en una base de platino."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1708
msgid "Warlord Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón de Caudillo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1709
msgid "Sovereign Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón Soberano"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1709
msgid ""
"Though soft and flexible, the material of this belt is made up of extremely fine strands of white gold.  The white gold is braided together by a process too exacting for human hands, and the ruby set into the buckle was perfectly cut by a process long lost in time."
msgstr ""
"Aunque es suave y flexible, el material de este cinturón está formado por finísimas hebras de oro blanco.  El oro blanco está trenzado mediante un proceso demasiado minucioso para manos humanas, y el rubí de la hebilla se talló a la perfección con un método perdido en el tiempo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:171
msgid "Serpent Wand of the Fist"
msgstr "Varita del Puño de Serpiente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1710
msgid "A used leather cloak.  It smells faintly of mothballs and dust."
msgstr "Una capa de cuero usada.  Huele levemente a naftalina y a polvo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1710
msgid "Leather Cloak"
msgstr "Capa de Cuero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1711
msgid ""
"Indigo dye from the Regnan Archipelago was used to stain this wool cloak the color of a summer night's sky."
msgstr ""
"Esta capa de lana se tiñó con añil del Archipiélago de Regna del color del cielo en una noche de verano."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1711
msgid "Phantom Cloak"
msgstr "Capa Fantasma"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1712
msgid "Elven Cloak"
msgstr "Capa Élfica"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1712
msgid ""
"Woven from plant fibers found in the forests of Erathia, these cloaks are the traditional garb of the Elven Rangers."
msgstr ""
"Tejidas con fibras vegetales de los bosques de Erathia, estas capas son el atuendo tradicional de los guardabosques élficos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1713
msgid ""
"A cloak formerly worn by high officials of the Church of the Sun of Karigor prior to the dissolution of the Church in 1083 A.S.  Nearly all these cloaks were enchanted in one way or another."
msgstr ""
"Una capa que vestían los altos cargos de la Iglesia del Sol de Karigor antes de la disolución de la Iglesia en el 1083 D.S.  Casi todas estas capas estaban encantadas de un modo u otro."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1713
msgid "Cardinal Cloak"
msgstr "Capa Cardenalicia"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1714
msgid ""
"A cloak formerly worn by high officials of the Church of the Moon of Karigor prior to the dissolution of the Church in 1083 A.S.  Nearly all these cloaks were enchanted in one way or another."
msgstr ""
"Una capa que vestían los altos cargos de la Iglesia de la Luna de Karigor antes de la disolución de la Iglesia en el 1083 D.S.  Casi todas estas capas estaban encantadas de un modo u otro."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1714
msgid "Doom's Day Cloak"
msgstr "Capa del Día del Juicio"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1715
msgid "A steel plated gauntlet of simple make and design."
msgstr "Un guantelete chapado en acero de factura y diseño sencillos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1716
msgid "Knight Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes de Caballero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1716
msgid ""
"This gauntlet is an improvement over the simple, inflexible steel gauntlets commonly worn by goblins and brigands.  The back of the hand and wrist are solid, while the jointing around the fingers is made of chain links to improve dexterity."
msgstr ""
"Este guantelete mejora los sencillos y rígidos guanteletes de acero que suelen llevar goblins y bribones.  El dorso de la mano y la muñeca son macizos, mientras que las articulaciones de los dedos son de malla para mejorar la destreza."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1717
msgid "Paladin Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes de Paladín"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1717
msgid ""
"While lacking in flexibility, this gauntlet has reinforced joints over the knuckles and at the base of the wrist."
msgstr ""
"Aunque le falta flexibilidad, este guantelete tiene articulaciones reforzadas sobre los nudillos y en la base de la muñeca."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1718
msgid ""
"A high quality gauntlet, it offers both flexibility and protection.  The joints are reinforced, yet are 'soft' enough to permit nearly normal hand motion."
msgstr ""
"Un guantelete de gran calidad que ofrece a la vez flexibilidad y protección.  Las articulaciones están reforzadas, pero son lo bastante «blandas» para permitir un movimiento de la mano casi normal."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1718
msgid "Cavalier Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes de Guerrero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1719
msgid ""
"Dwarven smiths created this masterpiece of gauntlet design.  Except for the extra bulk, there seems little difference between this gauntlet and a velvet glove.  Clever sliding and rotating plates at the joints and wrist permit full normal hand motion while providing continuous protection at all times."
msgstr ""
"Los herreros enanos crearon esta obra maestra del diseño de guanteletes.  Salvo por el volumen añadido, apenas parece haber diferencia entre este guantelete y un guante de terciopelo.  Ingeniosas placas deslizantes y giratorias en las articulaciones y la muñeca permiten mover la mano con total normalidad sin perder la protección en ningún momento."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1719
msgid "Ultimate Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes Supremos"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:172
msgid "Serpent Wand of Rocks"
msgstr "Varita de Rocas de Serpiente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1720
msgid ""
"Common traveler's boots made with leather and hobnailed. Their previous owner didn't maintain them very well, and the leather appears discolored and warped in places."
msgstr ""
"Botas de viajero corrientes, de cuero y con clavos en la suela. Su anterior dueño no las cuidó demasiado, y el cuero está descolorido y deformado en algunas partes."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1720
msgid "Old Leather Boots"
msgstr "Botas de Cuero Viejas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1721
msgid ""
"Heavy steel boots made for solid foot protection in battle.  They are uncomfortable to walk in and have a tendency to rust on the inside."
msgstr ""
"Pesadas botas de acero hechas para proteger bien los pies en la batalla.  Son incómodas para caminar y tienden a oxidarse por dentro."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1721
msgid "Steel Boots"
msgstr "Botas de Acero"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1722
msgid "Armored Boots"
msgstr "Botas Blindadas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1722
msgid ""
"The interior of these steel plated boots is made of leather and cloth to soften the sharp edges on the metal plates.  They are a bit heavy and exhausting to wear for extended periods."
msgstr ""
"El interior de estas botas chapadas en acero es de cuero y tela para suavizar los bordes afilados de las placas metálicas.  Pesan un poco y cansan si se llevan mucho tiempo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1723
msgid "Sterling Boots"
msgstr "Botas de Plata"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1724
msgid ""
"Dragonhide boots reinforced with molded horn strips and stalt metal rivets.  Soft and light, they provide unparalleled foot protection."
msgstr ""
"Botas de piel de dragón reforzadas con tiras de cuerno moldeado y remaches de stalt.  Blandas y ligeras, ofrecen una protección para los pies sin igual."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1724
msgid "Ultimate Boots"
msgstr "Botas Supremas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1725
msgid ""
"A small golden ring with a quarter carat diamond.  The style is simple and elegant."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño anillo de oro con un diamante de un cuarto de quilate.  El estilo es sencillo y elegante."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1725
msgid "Fine Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Fino"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1726
msgid "Sparkling Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Centelleante"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1726
msgid "Two amethysts adorn this plain platinum ring."
msgstr "Dos amatistas adornan este sencillo anillo de platino."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1727
msgid ""
"A gold ring with a large moonstone set in the center.  These rings typically carry an enchantment."
msgstr ""
"Un anillo de oro con una gran piedra lunar engastada en el centro.  Estos anillos suelen llevar un encantamiento."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1727
msgid "Lunar Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Lunar"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1728
msgid ""
"Rings such as this one were worn by the Witch's guild to signify membership during their heyday between 550-800 A.S."
msgstr ""
"Los miembros del Gremio de las Brujas llevaban anillos como este como signo de pertenencia durante su época de esplendor, entre el 550 y el 800 D.S."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1728
msgid "Witch Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de Bruja"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1729
msgid "Blessed Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Bendito"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1729
msgid ""
"The three pearls mounted on a gold base glimmer a faint blue when held out in the sun, offering insight as to the source of their magic."
msgstr ""
"Las tres perlas montadas sobre una base de oro brillan con un leve tono azul cuando se exponen al sol, lo que da una pista sobre el origen de su magia."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:173
msgid "Serpent Wand of Paralysis"
msgstr "Varita Paralizadora de Serpiente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1730
msgid ""
"A large star sapphire flanked by two smaller rubies decorate an otherwise plain gold band."
msgstr ""
"Un gran zafiro estrellado flanqueado por dos rubíes más pequeños decora un aro de oro por lo demás sencillo."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1730
msgid "Valuable Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Valioso"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1731
msgid "Precious Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Precioso"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1731
msgid ""
"Three gems, symmetrically equal in size and quality adorn a hammered gold band.  The center gem is a ruby, and the two flanking gems are purple topazes."
msgstr ""
"Tres gemas, simétricas e iguales en tamaño y calidad, adornan un aro de oro martillado.  La gema central es un rubí, y las dos de los lados son topacios morados."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1732
msgid ""
"A hammered white gold ring with a large central diamond and two small pearls, light doesn't fall upon it normally.  The ring glitters and fades unpredictably, as though it were lit by an invisible sun shining in an unseen, yet parallel world."
msgstr ""
"Un anillo de oro blanco martillado con un gran diamante central y dos pequeñas perlas; la luz no incide en él de forma normal.  El anillo centellea y se apaga de forma impredecible, como si lo iluminara un sol invisible que brillara en un mundo paralelo que no se ve."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1732
msgid "Ethereal Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Etéreo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1733
msgid "Exquisite Ring"
msgstr "Anillo Exquisito"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1733
msgid ""
"Three opals rimmed with a strange red metal are set in a perfect ring of stalt--a very rare metal found only in southern Erathia."
msgstr ""
"Tres ópalos ribeteados con un extraño metal rojo están engastados en un aro perfecto de stalt, un metal rarísimo que solo se encuentra en el sur de Erathia."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1734
msgid ""
"A gold band adorned with the shell of a rare beetle found only in the deserts of Enroth.  Treated properly by an alchemist, these shells can be made to hold the mightiest of enchantments."
msgstr ""
"Un aro de oro adornado con el caparazón de un escarabajo raro que solo se encuentra en los desiertos de Enroth.  Tratados como es debido por un alquimista, estos caparazones pueden albergar los encantamientos más poderosos."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1734
msgid "Scarab Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de Escarabajo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1735
msgid ""
"A turquoise stone bracketed by a bronze chain and clasp makes for an inexpensive, yet charming amulet."
msgstr ""
"Una piedra de turquesa sujeta por una cadena y un cierre de bronce forma un amuleto barato pero encantador."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1735
msgid "Turquoise Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto de Turquesa"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1736
msgid "Gothic Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto Gótico"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1736
msgid ""
"This bizarre amulet was probably created by some alchemist with a distorted understanding of magic.  The shape and symmetry help to maintain whatever enchantment he put in it."
msgstr ""
"Este extraño amuleto probablemente lo creó algún alquimista con una idea distorsionada de la magia.  Su forma y su simetría ayudan a mantener el encantamiento que le haya puesto."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1737
msgid "Claw Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto de Garra"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1737
msgid ""
"The ossified foot of some unknown beast or monster has been inset with a huge, imperfect purple topaz.  It's not pretty, but it's certainly magical."
msgstr ""
"En la pata osificada de alguna bestia o monstruo desconocido se ha engastado un enorme topacio morado imperfecto.  No es bonito, pero sin duda es mágico."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1738
msgid "Ancient Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto Antiguo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1738
msgid ""
"This amulet is composed of two pieces:  the front piece is an ancient, perfectly cut rectangle of a strong, stainless metal.  The backing is a much more recent gold chain and clasp.  Careful inspection of the front piece reveals it to be a plaque displaying the name of some long dead soldier or worker.  Symbols on the front probably indicate status and rank."
msgstr ""
"Este amuleto consta de dos piezas:  la delantera es un antiguo rectángulo, cortado a la perfección, de un metal resistente e inoxidable.  La trasera es una cadena con cierre de oro mucho más reciente.  Si se examina con atención, la pieza delantera resulta ser una placa con el nombre de algún soldado o trabajador muerto hace mucho.  Los símbolos del frente probablemente indican su posición y su rango."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1739
msgid ""
"A perfect ruby cut in a star shape and bracketed by a golden clasp give this amulet its name.  When viewed in dim light, a fiery spark can be seen dancing in the center of the gem."
msgstr ""
"Un rubí perfecto tallado en forma de estrella y sujeto por un cierre dorado da nombre a este amuleto.  Con poca luz, puede verse una chispa ardiente bailando en el centro de la gema."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1739
msgid "Ruby Star Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto de Estrella de Rubí"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:174
msgid "Serpent Wand of Clouds"
msgstr "Varita de Nubes de Serpiente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1740 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1741 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1742
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1743 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1744
msgid ""
"A rod of blue metal and wood capped with a blue headstone.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una vara de metal azul y madera rematada con una piedra azul.  Para usar esta varita, debéis equiparla como si fuera un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1740
msgid "Sparkling Wand of Fire"
msgstr "Varita Centelleante de Fuego"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1741
msgid "Sparkling Wand of Sparks"
msgstr "Varita Centelleante de Chispas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1742
msgid "Sparkling Wand of Poison"
msgstr "Varita Centelleante de Veneno"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1743
msgid "Sparkling Wand of Stunning"
msgstr "Varita Centelleante Aturdidora"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1744
msgid "Sparkling Wand of Harming"
msgstr "Varita Centelleante Dañina"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1745
msgid "Druid Wand of Light"
msgstr "Varita Druídica de Luz"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1745 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1746 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1747
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1748 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1749
msgid ""
"More a staff than a wand, this fairy wand is inexplicably alive, even though it was cut from its parent tree many years ago.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Más bastón que varita, esta varita feérica sigue inexplicablemente viva, aunque se cortó de su árbol hace muchos años.  Para usar esta varita, debéis equiparla como si fuera un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1746
msgid "Druid Wand of Ice"
msgstr "Varita Druídica de Hielo"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1747
msgid "Druid Wand of Lashing"
msgstr "Varita Druídica Azotadora"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1748
msgid "Druid Wand of Mind"
msgstr "Varita Druídica de la Mente"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1749
msgid "Druid Wand of Swarms"
msgstr "Varita Druídica de Enjambres"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:175 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:176 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:177
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:178 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:179
msgid ""
"A unicorn horn capped with a gold set ruby and crowned with a sculpted skull, this wand could only be the creation of the Necromancers' Guild. To use it you must equip it like a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un cuerno de unicornio rematado con un rubí engastado en oro y coronado con una calavera esculpida: esta varita solo puede ser obra del Gremio de los Nigromantes. Para usarla, debéis equiparla como un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:175
msgid "Necrotic Wand of Implosion"
msgstr "Varita Necrótica de Implosión"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1750
msgid "Cruel Wand of Fireballs"
msgstr "Varita Cruel de Bolas de Fuego"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1750 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1751 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1752
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1753 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1754
msgid ""
"Made from the hollowed out horn of a unicorn and spitted on a piece of polished wood, wands like these are born of cruelty and evil.  The enchantment it holds is useful;  the only real question is whether you believe your cause justifies the use of an item so wickedly created.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Hechas con el cuerno hueco de un unicornio ensartado en un trozo de madera pulida, las varitas como esta nacen de la crueldad y el mal.  El encantamiento que contiene es útil;  la única duda real es si creéis que vuestra causa justifica el uso de un objeto creado con tanta maldad.  Para usar esta varita, debéis equiparla como si fuera un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1751
msgid "Cruel Wand of Acid"
msgstr "Varita Cruel de Ácido"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1752
msgid "Cruel Wand of Lightning"
msgstr "Varita Cruel de Relámpagos"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1753
msgid "Cruel Wand of Blades"
msgstr "Varita Cruel de Cuchillas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1754
msgid "Cruel Wand of Berzerking"
msgstr "Varita Cruel de Frenesí"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1755
msgid "Arcane Wand of Blasting"
msgstr "Varita Arcana Explosiva"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1755 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1756 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1757
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1758 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1759
msgid ""
"Made of a reddish metal, the egg of a cockatrice fixed to the business end caps a wand containing a mighty enchantment.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Hecha de un metal rojizo, esta varita, rematada en su extremo activo con un huevo de cocatriz, contiene un poderoso encantamiento.  Para usar esta varita, debéis equiparla como si fuera un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1756
msgid "Arcane Wand of the Fist"
msgstr "Varita Arcana del Puño"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1757
msgid "Arcane Wand of Rocks"
msgstr "Varita Arcana de Rocas"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1758
msgid "Arcane Wand of Paralyzing"
msgstr "Varita Arcana Paralizadora"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1759
msgid "Arcane Wand of Clouds"
msgstr "Varita Arcana de Nubes"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:176
msgid "Necrotic Wand of Distortion"
msgstr "Varita Necrótica de Distorsión"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1760
msgid "Dragon Wand of Implosion"
msgstr "Varita de Dragón de Implosión"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1760 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1761 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1762
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1763 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1764
msgid ""
"Formed of the clawed forepaw of a baby dragon, wands like this one can hold the strongest of spells.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Hechas con la garra delantera de una cría de dragón, las varitas como esta pueden albergar los hechizos más fuertes.  Para usar esta varita, debéis equiparla como si fuera un arma."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1761
msgid "Dragon Wand of Distortion"
msgstr "Varita de Dragón de Distorsión"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1762
msgid "Dragon Wand of Shrapmetal"
msgstr "Varita de Dragón de Metralla"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1763
msgid "Dragon Wand of Shrinking"
msgstr "Varita de Dragón Reductora"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1764
msgid "Dragon Wand of Incineration"
msgstr "Varita de Dragón de Incineración"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1765
msgid ""
"A magical herb of unusual properties.  Popppysnaps can be used to make potions.  (To use, pick the herb up and right-click over an empty potion bottle.)"
msgstr ""
"Una hierba mágica de propiedades inusuales.  Las Cápsulas de Amapola sirven para preparar pociones.  (Para usarla, coged la hierba y haced clic derecho sobre un Frasco de Poción vacío.)"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1765 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1766 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1767
